,"text":"With "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumCardinality"},{"type":"text","text":", the heaviest among the maximum-cardinality matchings; without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it, a negative edge is never taken and a zero-weight one may be. Among parallel edges, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"heaviest copy is used (the earliest on ties). Self-loops are never weighed; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"called once per other edge, in position order. Integer arithmetic is exact."}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(n³)."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Complexity"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every |weight| ≤ "},{"code":"W.max \/ 8","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and n · |weight| ≤ "},{"code":"W.max \/ 8","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"maximumCardinality","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (its duals go negative, by up to about n times the greatest weight);"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the total weight fits in "},{"code":"W","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Beyond that, arithmetic may overflow, which traps."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Precondition"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule","doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Edges-swift.associatedtype":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph\/edges-swift.associatedtype","abstract":[],"title":"Edges","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype